# The nightly every app here was checked under, and the manifest's `compiler`
# line. Upstream's own `.roc-version` at this tag is nightly-2026-09-01-db83307.
#
# 0.9.0 changes only upstream's CI and docs tooling. package/ and examples/ are
# byte-identical to 0.8.0, and the release tarball keeps the same content hash,
# so the repin changes the URL's tag and nothing else. The topics pin
# basic-cli 0.24.0, which does not pass the program name in `args`.
compiler nightly-2026-10-06-c34079d

index.json  <- package/, parsed by `roc-syntax-mcp plugin index`. Public and
               private modules; `package [...]` in main.roc is what separates
               them. No source is vendored
examples/   <- examples/, repinned in two steps. First, two edits per file. Upstream
               pins weaver as `../package/main.roc`, a path that resolves only
               inside a checkout, so each header's weaver entry is replaced with
               the 0.9.0 tarball above; and each file gains one `##` line above
               its header, because that line is the title
               `list_roc_index(kind: "examples")` prints and upstream's examples
               carry none. Two filenames gain an underscore, because the gate
               reads one flat `<dir>/*.roc`: default-values.roc and
               single-arg.roc. Second, patches/0001 moves every example off
               upstream's platform, lukewilliamboswell/roc-platform-template-zig
               1.0.0, onto basic-cli 0.24.0. That template's Stdout, Stdin and
               Stderr warn "redundant open tag union" under the nightly above,
               as does its 1.1.0, and the gate reads a warning as a failure.
               Per file: the `pf` URL, `import pf.OsStr`, `main!` takes
               `List(OsStr)`, `args` is passed whole (basic-cli 0.24.0 already
               drops the program name) with `OsStr.to_raw` as the converter, and
               the now-unused `str_to_raw_arg` adapter is deleted. Drop the patch
               once a template release builds clean.
topics/     <- this package's own, not upstream's: programs written against
               this pin and declared in plugin.json so they answer by name. They
               pin basic-cli 0.24.0, as the patched examples do, because
               that is the platform this server ships and the one a reader is
               most likely writing against.
overview.md <- this package's own. Every API claim on it was compiled, and every
               fenced block appears in verify/overview-snippets.roc.

